  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.engineer_notes.1": "The Spire Main leaves this hall and runs straight to the Chronospire. We laid it true: even broken, the pipe still points home.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.engineer_notes.2": "Every phase of the Spire was tuned against this engine. Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight: four strokes of a single heart.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.engineer_notes.3": "Should the Heartgear stop, the Spire will keep turning on its own memory. But it will forget the hands that wound it.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.foreman_log.1": "Day 212. Pressure holds at the third gauge. The Horologists came again with their brass charts and asked for more flow toward the Spire.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.foreman_log.2": "They say their tower turns with the days of the world below, and that it must drink to keep its hours. We send it what the clouds give us.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.foreman_log.3": "Day 240. The Heartgear stutters. The vault is flooded with stagnant mist and sealed until the clockmakers answer.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.foreman_log.4": "Should anyone need the vault: three drain valves feed the regulator. One in the west tank, one on the north gantry, one here in my office. Open all three.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.vault_letter.1": "If you read this, the mist is gone and the regulator still obeys. Good. The plans in this vault are ours.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.vault_letter.2": "Kairite turns their gears. Mine it when the vein pulses brightest, or you will only gather dust.",
  "book.upfall.stalled_engine.vault_letter.3": "Carry the plans to a smithing table. And if you climb the Chronospire, tell it the engine is stalled, not dead.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.horologist_letter.1": "To the Horologists of the Spire. Your last shipment of brass arrived intact; our thanks. Our vaults keep time poorly, but you have taught us to count it.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.horologist_letter.2": "You asked what we store. Weight, friends. The weight of falling. We fold a room into a point and set the point in a cube, and the room forgets it was ever heavy.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.horologist_letter.3": "Should our work go wrong, follow the lattice beams; we laid them toward the nearest archive. Trust them more than your eyes.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.horologist_letter.4": "Send no more brass. Send a clock tuned to a stranger day. We would like to know how long a Tilt lasts.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.surveyor_journal.1": "Third survey, first day of the Fold. We stack space like folded linen and store the weight of the world in lattice vaults. A cube holds what a mountain cannot.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.surveyor_journal.2": "The sky builders lent us their pearlstone and their patience. They ask only that we never fold a city. We have promised. Promises weigh little here.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.surveyor_journal.3": "The Fold pushes. Every vault we close shoves the land a little farther off. The islands drift from us, or we from them. The warden says it is the same thing.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.surveyor_journal.4": "Tomorrow we attempt the Tilt: the whole reliquary turned an eighth of a circle, so the weight runs down the diagonal. Forgive the shaking of my hand.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.warden_note.1": "The Tilt held for one breath. Then every vault shattered mid-fold and stopped, tilted, exactly as you see them. Nothing fell. Nothing could.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.warden_note.2": "The Fold pushed us out beyond every island, which is why none of you came. The core still hums. It opens only for what made it: four Fold Shards.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.warden_note.3": "One shard rests in each satellite that circles the heart. Set all four in the sockets of the sealed walls before you approach the heart. A socket cannot be emptied again.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.warden_note.4": "When the fourth sits true, the seals will dissolve and the heart will stand open. Within lies our last tool, the Fold Anchor. It remembers a place for half a minute.",
  "book.upfall.tilted_reliquary.warden_note.5": "Anchor yourself, step where you must, and the Fold will bring you back. Use it well. Do not fold a city.",
